WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.801
-Sarah, how are you?

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.802
-Hi. Good.
Yeah. Thanks.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.403
How you doing?
-I'm doing well.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.939
This is the longest-distance
interview

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.742
we have done since
social distancing started.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:10.977
You're in Australia right now.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.179
Thank you for waking up
so early to do this.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.281
-I am, I am.
It's not too bad.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.584
It's like 9:00 a.m.
It's fine.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.853
It's a regular workday.
It's a regular workday.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.289
-It is a regular workday.
And I should --

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.526
I want to congratulate you
for your Emmy nomination

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:30.230
for "Succession," but because of
the time difference,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.398
that must have happened in the
middle of the night for you.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:33.933
Are you the kind of person
who sets an alarm

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.870
to find out if this happened?
-No.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.971
[ Laughs ] No.
I totally --

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.573
My manager asked
if I wanted to be woken up,

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.374
I was like, "No.
It's like 2:00 in the morning.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:44.711
I'll sleep. Either I've been
nominated or I haven't.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.912
It's not gonna change
whether I wake up or not."

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:49.348
No, I got woken up by my friend

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.517
who I'm living with
at the moment in lockdown.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.586
And they ran into the room
and pulled the pillow

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.222
off my head and said, "You've
been nominated for an Emmy!"

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.092
And, yeah, it was a pretty
good way to find out.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.526
-That's a great way to find out.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.661
You know, I was talking to --

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.129
Matthew Macfadyen
was on the show.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.232
He obviously is fantastic
playing your husband, Tom.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.901
And he was saying one of
the disappointing things,

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.237
the depressing things, one
of the many depressing things,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.006
but you guys won't be able
to celebrate together

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:15.675
at a virtual Emmys.
Is that a bummer?

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.545
-Yeah, it is.
It is, because I miss everybody.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.679
And, you know,
I want to be working again.

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:23.015
And everyone's in the same boat,
globally,

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.083
no matter the industry.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.251
Everyone wants
to get back to work,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.753
to be social
and with their friends.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.855
But I feel like
we've got such a great team

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.258
and have such a great chemistry
on and off screen that,

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.961
yeah, it's a shame not to be
able to do that all together,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.497
particularly for so many of us
being nominated at the Emmys.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.465
It's -- It's wild.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.368
-I also want to point out that I
was lucky enough to meet you

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.371
last year, like,
the night-before party.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.973
And the whole "Succession" cast,

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.442
not just yourself
but all of you,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.377
you guys were like
the hot people

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.611
that everybody
wanted to talk to.

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:54.680
-[ Laughing ]
-Everybody wanted to come up --

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.483
'Cause I felt like, right as
the Emmys was hitting last year

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.819
was when everyone had finally
caught up to the show.

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:03.155
It was cresting
just at the right time.

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:07.460
-It was pretty, in some ways,
confronting, I guess, for me,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.229
because I really didn't expect
to go to the Emmys last year

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:13.132
and, like, slip under the radar,
not be seen,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.567
just work out
what it's all about.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.135
"Okay,
that's a very famous person,

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.670
there's another one,
I'm from Australia,

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.340
just be cool, chill out."

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.074
But then, when they all started
coming up to me and going,

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:26.546
"Hey, I love your work!"
yeah, that -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:31.451
-I do feel like now everybody
is thirsting for a third season,

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.486
whereas the second season
maybe caught people

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:36.088
a little by surprise.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:39.959
Obviously, you're thirsting
for a third season, as well.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.195
Is there --
I mean, you hear whispers

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.097
that it's maybe
gonna start in the winter?

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.399
-Uh...yes?

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.402
I mean, I want to get back
as soon as possible.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.869
And in a couple months' time,
that will happen.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:52.772
But I think everything changes
so fast at the moment

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.940
that you can say it's October,

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.510
and it'll end up being
sometime later because,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.878
you know,
we don't know.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.881
-It's good that you guys,
as a cast,

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.851
are taking
the pandemic seriously,

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.755
because I don't think a single
character on the show would.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:11.757
-No.
Well, only in the way of, like,

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.894
constantly hand-sanitizing
and just isolating themselves

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.897
way ahead of any advice
to isolate.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.832
You know, and they've got
their summer palace.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.233
They wouldn't even have
to isolate together.

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:24.069
They could all have a house
or a ranch to themselves.

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.505
Yeah, but they probably would
want to isolate together

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:27.607
in some ways just in case

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.375
somebody made some moves
or positioning.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.377
-Right.
Just to keep eyes on them.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.513
Has the show
taken off in Australia?

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:38.250
Because some might even say
it's based on Australians.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.121
-It has taken off in a way
that I feel it's still, like,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.790
what first season was
in America.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.292
Like, there's still a bit
of word of mouth going on.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.194
It's on a TV channel --

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:53.499
Like, it's on Foxtel
and on Binge now, I think.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.635
So, it's -- it's there.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:58.971
But it's still simmering,
which is nice. Yeah.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.540
-You did find out on Halloween
that it was

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.942
slightly more popular
than you had known.

00:04:03.942 --> 00:04:05.878
-[ Laughing ] I did, yes.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.248
I keep getting tagged
in photographs that sort of

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.950
jarred me a little, to go,
"Oh, that's not me.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.154
That's not me. That's a --
That's a terrible red wig.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.689
But it's meant to be me.
Okay.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.792
That's just paper-bag pants and
a turtleneck with a gold chain.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.994
That's "you didn't know you
would be going to this

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.829
Halloween party
and you just found that

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.698
in your closet
and you made a costume."

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.700
My favorite was --
-But it was funny to hear that

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.837
and realize, "Oh, yeah,
Shiv does have a very

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:36.108
iconic style that you could
also not have to do

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:39.111
a ton of planning for
but also nail the Shiv look.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:43.049
But this is a style you sort of
brought to the character, yes?

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:46.051
-Yes. I mean,
I wear high-waisted pants

00:04:46.051 --> 00:04:48.687
and sort of a wider-leg pant,
I guess.

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:52.291
But there's no way in which
I am stylish as Sarah.

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.427
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.328
Any style I brought
to the character

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:58.798
was cherry-picked
from other things

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:02.535
and put together by Michelle
far more than it was me.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.903
Yeah.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:07.206
-I do want to provide you
this opportunity, before we go,

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.042
to clear up an Internet rumor
about your birthday.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.913
-[ Laughing ] Oh, yes.
Please.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.381
I'm a proud Sagittarian.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.850
I am not born July 28th.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.918
My birthday's
the 1st of December.

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:22.121
Someone made
a Wikipedia page up for me,

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:26.325
and they just decided
that 28th of July was me.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.626
And so,
for a couple of years now,

00:05:27.626 --> 00:05:30.930
I've been getting happy
unbirthdays from friends.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.198
And even my agent actually
wished me a happy birthday once

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:34.967
a couple years ago.
-It's nice, though.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.403
I feel like it's a good way
to distinguish your real friends

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.071
from your friends
who just sort of

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:41.340
are living off Internet
knowledge of you.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.308
-Oh, 100%.
Yeah.

00:05:43.308 --> 00:05:46.512
When I get a happy birthday from
someone who's maybe not

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.214
in the know, I'm like, "Okay.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.049
Well, we need to work
on this friendship.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.784
I need to let you in
a little closer.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.352
Maybe it's my fault
that I haven't told you

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:56.188
my birthday is December the 1st.
-That's very helpful.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.357
I'm thinking of planting
a poison pill

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:01.293
fake birthday myself now
on my Internet page,

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:04.830
just so I can separate
the posers from the real deal.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.366
-Yeah. I mean, it's lucky
that I'm only six months out.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:10.603
But I feel like, if I was gonna
fake my own birthday,

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.904
I should've gone, you know,

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.440
three, four years,
five years earlier.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.942
-Yeah, that's true.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.877
That's, I guess,
how we know you didn't do it.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.879
-Yeah, it's true.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:22.715
-Congratulations again
on the nomination.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.151
Thank you.
Again, it's 9:00 a.m.,

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:27.386
but for a lot of actors,
that's a big deal.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:30.489
So we will say thank you.
And, uh...

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:32.157
-I'm going back to bed,
to be honest.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:33.759
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:36.562
-Always great to see you, Sarah.
-Good to see you.

